CKBuilder Week 1 — OffCKB devnet session
Date: 2026-08-26
Host: Windows 10 Pro 19045, Node v22.16.0, npm 10.9.2
Note: private keys redacted. The devnet keys used here are the well-known
      prefunded OffCKB development keys and hold no real value.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Confirm the real package name before installing anything globally
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

$ npm view offckb name version description homepage
name = 'offckb'
version = '1.0.0'
description = 'Placeholder package for offckb - reserved name'
homepage = 'https://github.com/yourusername/offckb-placeholder#readme'

$ npm view @offckb/cli name version description homepage
name = '@offckb/cli'
version = '0.4.13'
description = 'ckb development network for your first try'
homepage = 'https://github.com/ckb-devrel/offckb#readme'

--> the docs are right, @offckb/cli is the real one. See
    notes/findings/offckb-install-observations.md

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Install
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

$ npm install -g @offckb/cli
added 133 packages in 19s

$ offckb --version
0.4.13

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Start the devnet
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

$ offckb node
The system cannot find the path specified.
CKB Binary not found, download and install the new version 0.208.0..
Failed to detect CPU features, using portable binary {"code":"MODULE_NOT_FOUND","requireStack":["...\\@offckb\\cli\\build\\index.js"]}
downloading https://github.com/nervosnetwork/ckb/releases/download/v0.208.0/ckb_v0.208.0_x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip ..
CKB 0.208.0 installed successfully.
Launching CKB devnet Node...
CKB devnet is ready at http://127.0.0.1:8114.
Follow the full node log with: offckb logs -f
CKB devnet RPC Proxy server running on http://127.0.0.1:28114

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Confirm the chain is actually producing blocks
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

$ curl -s -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
    -d '{"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"get_tip_block_number","params":[]}' \
    http://127.0.0.1:8114
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":"0x2","id":1}

